<BaseLayout
  title="About — PokéTFT"
  description="About the PokéTFT project and this devlog."
>
  <div class="page">
    <div class="about-header">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        PokéTFT is a passion project: a fully custom auto-battler built in the
        Pokemon universe. The combat engine, unit kits, trait systems, and
        economy are all being designed and coded from scratch.
      </p>

      <h2>What this blog is</h2>
      <p>
        This devlog covers the design decisions behind the game — the thinking
        that happens before and after the code. Why a given Pokemon belongs in a
        trait, how I translate an ability from the mainline games into a
        competitive auto-battler kit, how traits are structured so their bonuses
        are meaningful at every threshold.
      </p>
      <p>
        It's also a record of what didn't work, what had to be rethought, and
        what surprised me along the way.
      </p>

      <h2>About me</h2>
      <p>
        <!-- Add your own bio here -->
        I'm a developer and Pokemon fan who's been playing TFT since its release.
        At some point "I could design a better Pokemon version of this" turned
        into actually building one.
      </p>

      <h2>Follow along</h2>
      <p>
        The game and blog are both works in progress. The best way to follow
        along is to bookmark this site — new posts go up as design decisions get
        made.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
